---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Every week you push one scenario draft further through the same
    pipeline a working Keeper uses: a spark of interest becomes a premise,
    the premise gets fused with a Mythos truth and antagonist, a structure
    gets committed to, and then clues, puzzles, checks and NPCs get built
    on top of it so the thing survives contact with a real table. You'll
    run an actual playtest of your own draft partway through the semester
    and revise it in response. You walk out with a complete, playtested
    Call of Cthulhu scenario another Keeper could pick up and run cold.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    You should already know how to play a tabletop RPG as a player or
    Keeper — this course doesn't teach dice mechanics or how a session
    runs. It doesn't require prior Mythos knowledge or a background in
    creative writing; what it asks for is a willingness to run a real
    playtest with real players partway through semester, using either
    your own group or the studio's playtest-matching arrangement.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
